From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 17:39:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ux): the space bar, and rename the assistant to
 EcowoodsGuide
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Reported as "the chat widget won't let me type spaces". The chat widget was
innocent — its input handles nothing but Enter.

THE SPACE BAR WAS BROKEN ON THE WHOLE HOMEPAGE

FloorCatalog and MachineCatalog each registered a window-level keydown listener
that called preventDefault() on the space bar to toggle a carousel, and
intercepted both arrow keys. A window listener fires regardless of focus. Both
components are mounted on home-client.tsx. The homepage carries the primary
lead-capture form.

So on the highest-traffic page of a business whose funnel is "type your project
into this box", the space bar did nothing and the arrow keys jumped a carousel
instead of moving the text cursor. A customer typing "White oak, main floor,
about 600 square feet" got "Whiteoak,mainfloor,about600squarefeet".

This is the most expensive bug found in this engagement. A wrong price loses an
argument; this loses the lead before there is an argument to have.

lib/keyboard.ts now owns one definition of "is a person typing here".
whenNotTyping() wraps a global handler so it ignores input, textarea, select,
contentEditable and role=textbox/combobox, while still delivering Escape.
CommandPalette had hand-rolled the same check and had it nearly right — it
missed select and the ARIA roles — and now uses the shared predicate.

pnpm seo:keys fails the build on any window/document key listener that calls
preventDefault without consulting that module. It found the CommandPalette case
on its first run. This class of bug is invisible to typecheck, to the build and
to every other guard here, so it gets its own.

RENOGUIDE → ECOWOODSGUIDE

The name was a literal in nineteen places, and it was the wrong name. Every
other surface on this site is relentlessly one entity — schema graph, llms.txt,
ai.txt, the citation guide — and then the one thing a visitor actually talks to
introduced itself as a second brand, in the highest-intent moment on the site.

lib/assistant-identity.ts is the single source. lib/renoguide.ts →
lib/assistant.ts, openRenoGuide → openAssistant, RENOGUIDE_OPEN_EVENT →
ASSISTANT_OPEN_EVENT, RENOGUIDE_SYSTEM_PROMPT → ECOWOODS_GUIDE_SYSTEM_PROMPT.

The greeting was rewritten with it: it used to ask for species, square footage
and area before offering anything, which is a form with a chat interface painted
on it. Someone whose floor is cupping does not know their square footage. And
the second chip is now "My floor is cupping or gapping" — the largest group of
people who open a flooring chat window have a floor that is already
misbehaving, and the widget had nothing to say to them.

EVERY REPLY CLOSES ON ECOWOODS

The system prompt now requires every reply — including answers to questions
with nothing to do with buying — to end on the specific service or next step
that follows from what was just said, with the symptom→service mapping written
out and the offer listed by name so it stops being paraphrased into vagueness.
A reply that answers the question and stops is a failed reply.

pnpm seo:assistant fails on the retired name, on the current name typed as a
literal, or on the always-close rule being trimmed out of the prompt.

VERIFICATION

tsc: 107 errors, identical set to baseline. One was introduced and fixed — an
escaped backtick broke the prompt's template literal, which surfaced as eight
parse errors and a LOWER total, worth remembering: a falling error count can
mean the compiler stopped early. All 27 verify:* pass. All 11 seo gates pass.

